 "provenance_complete": true,
 "note": "baselines are not part of the framework and are not held to R2/R4 (\u00a712.4). Detector IV is a population-marginal estimator, NOT an isolation forest: the \u00a712.4 comparison is between independent models, not framework-against-its-own-component. The category census is the sharper statement of why they differ \u2014 no labelled event is a population-marginal outlier, which is a property of the attacks rather than of any model. Seven of the eight models here are population-scope and share that blind spot by construction; entity_ewma is the one that does not, and it is the baseline the framework has to beat to show that its calibration machinery earns its place above the per-entity framing alone"
}